SELECT define_provision($q$RRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2015@2025-03-28$q$, $q$Table 6.2.3.3.2 AO7.1$q$, 'ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME', $q$AO7.1
Minimum setbacks are in accordance with the following:
- buildings are set back from the street frontage in accordance with Table 6.2.3.3.3;
- the side boundary setback is a minimum of:
- 1.5 metres for a wall up to 8.5 metres high;
- 2.5 metres for a wall up to twelve (12) metres high; and
- 3.5 metres for any part of a wall over twenty (20) metres high; and
- the rear boundary setback is four (4) metres unless to a laneway being one (1) metre at ground storey and 0.5 metres above ground level. || Table 6.2.3.3.3 — Minimum building setback from street frontage || Building height | Front setback – building | Front setback – balconies || Basement | 0 metres | N/A || Storeys 1 – 3. | Within twenty (20) per cent of the average front setback of adjoining buildings; OR Where there are no adjoining buildings — three (3) metres. | 1.5 metres || Four (4) storeys and above. | Five (5) metres. | 3 metres$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$Section 101, Table 6.2.3.3.2 PO7/AO7.1; Table 6.2.3.3.3$q$, NULL, $q$High density residential zone code$q$, NULL, $q$https://rockeplan.rockhamptonregion.qld.gov.au/eplan/rules/0/101/0/0/0/49$q$, $q$SC1.2 'Setback': 'For a building or structure, means the shortest distance, measured horizontally, between the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the boundary of the lot where the building or structure is.'$q$, $q$rrc_hdr_assessable_front$q$);
