SELECT define_provision($q$RRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2015@2025-03-28$q$, $q$Table 8.2.5.3.1 AO8.1.1$q$, 'ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT', $q$AO8.1.1
Car ports, garages and other enclosed outbuildings are:
- located behind the main face of the dwelling house; or
- set back an equal or greater distance from the street as the main building and do not have a garage door or solid face presented to the street.
OR || AO8.1.2
Where an open car port is located in the front of the main building, the car port:
- is detached from the main building;
- has a maximum width of 3.6 metres;
- has a maximum height of four (4) metres above ground level;
- has a pitched roof (pyramidal, hip or gable or any combination of pyramidal, hip or gable) with a minimum of fifteen (15) degrees roof pitch or a pitch equal to that of the main dwelling house or building;
- has a minimum roof overhang of thirty (30) centimetres;
- has roofing material consistent with the roofing material used on the main dwelling house or building; and
- has a gutter profile consistent with the gutter profile used on the main dwelling house or building.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$Section 67 (8.2.5 Character overlay code), rule 3027, Table 8.2.5.3.1 PO8/AO8.1$q$, NULL, $q$Character overlay code$q$, NULL, $q$https://rockeplan.rockhamptonregion.qld.gov.au/eplan/rules/0/67/0/0/0/49$q$, $q$SC1.2 'Setback': 'For a building or structure, means the shortest distance, measured horizontally, between the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the boundary of the lot where the building or structure is.'$q$, $q$rrc_character_outbuilding_front$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "RRC.rrc_character_outbuilding_front", "instrument_version": "RRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2015@2025-03-28", "topic": "SETBACK.FRONTAGE", "title": "Table 8.2.5.3.1 AO8.1.1", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_FRONT", "operator": ">=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "outbuilding street setback >= main building street setback", "extracted_value": null, "extracted_operator": "conditional"}, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2025-03-28", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "ROCKHAMPTON"}, {"level": "OVERLAY", "overlay": "RRC:OV:CHARACTER_OVERLAY_RESIDENTIAL_CHARACTER_DESIGN_CONTROL_AREA_OM_5"}], "subjects": ["CLASS_10A"], "sources": [{"key": "rrc_character_outbuilding_front", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"front setback of car ports, garages and enclosed outbuildings\", \"operator\": \"conditional\", \"value\": null, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"land in the Residential character design control area only\", \"located behind the main face of the dwelling house; or\", \"set back an equal or greater distance from the street as the main building and no garage door or solid face presented to the street\"], \"exceptions\": [\"AO8.1.2: an open car port may be located in front of the main building if detached, max 3.6 m wide, max 4 m high, pitched roof etc.\"], \"formula_text\": \"outbuilding street setback >= main building street setback\"}\nStructure scope 'Car ports, garages and other enclosed outbuildings' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_10A']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES - Part 1 s1.6 Table 1.6.1: 'Alternative provisions to the QDC MP1.1 and QDC MP1.2 for a class 1 and 10 building or structure' -> 'Character overlay code' (Sections 32(b), 32(c) and 33 BA and section 10 BR)\nResearcher notes: Table 5.9.5: in the Residential character design control area a dwelling house MCU (accepted in any zone) and building work for extensions, external alterations or minor building work are 'Accepted subject to requirements' against this code. AO1.1 (front setback within 20% of adjoining average) expressly excludes car ports, garages and other enclosed outbuildings, so is not recorded."}$q$::jsonb);
